course: dictionary
lesson: 7987
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The dictionary gives them as 1) and 2). Context, the words around the word, tells you which meaning the writer means. Recreation is one of these words.
explain: Meaning 1 is things people do for fun and relaxation in their free time, like sport, games and hobbies. At the rec, which is short for the recreation ground (a public park), Big Gaz from Year 8 grabs Sam's new ball and shouts «Go fetch, little man.» The rec is a place for play, so recreation here means fun and free time.
explain: Meaning 2 is making something again, or a copy of something old. It is pronounced re-create-ion, and the hyphen in re-creation helps you see the parts: re- (again) and create (make). A re-creation of a Viking village is built to look like the old one.
fact: Recreation means things people do for fun and relaxation in their free time.
fact: The recreation ground, or «the rec», is a public park where people go to play.
fact: Recreation time at school means break time.
fact: Recreation can also mean making something again, or a copy of something old: a re-creation.
fact: The re- in re-creation can mean again, so a re-creation is something made again.
exercise: «Big Gaz from Year 8 grabs Sam's new ball at the rec.» What is the rec? | A shop that sells balls | A cinema in town | A school hall | *A public park where people play
exercise: Our class visits a re-creation of a Viking village. What does re-creation mean here? | A map of the river | *A copy of something old, made again | Fun and games in free time | A very old village that is still lived in
exercise: Which of these is an example of recreation, meaning fun and relaxation in free time? | *Playing football with friends at the weekend | Filing away old papers | Sitting a spelling test in silence | Doing homework at the kitchen table
test: Mum says the weekend is for recreation. What does she mean? | Cleaning the car all day | Doing extra maths homework | *Free time for fun, games and hobbies | Copying old letters by hand
test: The museum has a re-creation of a Roman bath. What is a re-creation? | A brand new invention | A kind of sports game | *A copy made again of something old | A rubbish tip
exam: The sign says «recreation centre». What does the word suggest? | A museum of old things | A school exam hall | *A place for fun, sport and free-time activities | Making something again
